        "text": "Prior/update/interval: base rate/reference class is same-series CPS unemployment, seasonally adjusted, with the recent official April-October 2026 level history [4.3, 4.3, 4.2, 4.1, 4.1, 4.2, 4.1]. I use a one-month persistence prior from October 2026 at 4.1, cross-checked against the seven-month mean of 4.1857 and longer same-series anchors including November 2024 at 4.2 and November 2025 at 4.5. Level adjustment is 0.0 because the series is already close to the recent mean; momentum adjustment is 0.0 because the last six changes alternate around flat; one-off adjustment is 0.0 because no source-valid discrete rebenchmark belongs in this November first print. Interval method uses successive changes: diff(history) = [0.0, -0.1, -0.1, 0.0, 0.1, -0.1], sigma = 0.08164965809277289, and 1.28*sigma = 0.1045115623587493. For one-decimal official reporting and labor-market regime risk, I widen modestly from 4.1 +/- 0.1045 to an 80% interval of 4.0 to 4.3."
